1. Eligible users and permitted purpose

An accredited university or other institution of higher education, and its
enrolled students and personnel acting within that institution's teaching
or research activities, may download, install, run, study and internally
modify this software solely for teaching and noncommercial academic research.
The permission is nonexclusive, worldwide and royalty-free, subject to these
terms. Research institutes that are not institutions of higher education,
companies and unaffiliated individuals require separate written permission.

Noncommercial academic research excludes development or validation of a
commercial product or service, paid consulting, production deployment,
commercial network operation, and work undertaken for the commercial benefit
of a third party. Ordinary university tuition and general research grants do
not, by themselves, make teaching or research commercial. Commercially
commissioned product research requires separate written permission.

2. Internal copies and modifications

Eligible users may make copies and modifications within their institution
only as necessary for the permitted purpose. Preserve this license and all
copyright and attribution notices. Clearly identify changes in internal
modified versions. Recipients within the institution must be made aware of
these terms. This license does not transfer ownership of modifications.

3. Publication and redistribution

Except for the hosting-platform rights in section 4, redistribution of this
software or substantial portions of it, publication of modified versions,
sublicensing, and transfer to another institution or third party require the
copyright holder's prior written permission. Direct other eligible users to
the official repository instead of redistributing a copy.

Users may publish papers, evaluation results, independently written algorithms
and generated numerical data from permitted research, provided they do not
include restricted source code or substantial portions of the software.
This license does not claim ownership of those independent research outputs.
Academic acknowledgement of ChannelHub and applicable upstream tools is
requested in research publications.

4. Public hosting platform

Where this software is hosted in a public GitHub repository, nothing in this
license purports to limit rights that the copyright holder grants under
GitHub's applicable Terms of Service, including viewing and forking within
GitHub as permitted by its functionality. That platform-required permission
does not grant additional commercial-use or off-platform redistribution rights
under this license. It does not imply endorsement of any fork.

5. Other rights and third-party components

No use outside the permission above is granted. No trademark or express
patent license is granted by this document. Separately licensed third-party
components remain subject to their own licenses; this license does not
restrict rights granted directly by their copyright holders. See the
